FILE: vUX-prompt.js
FEATURE: prompt-module
DATE: 2026-11-09
PRIOR STATE: as left by the last commit plus uncommitted work from earlier features

REASON
NEW FILE. The Prompt module: Promise-based alert(), confirm() and input() dialogs,
so apps stop using the blocking, unstyled window.alert/confirm/prompt.

Design points worth recording:
  - Native <dialog> + showModal(): top layer above every z-index (ModalDisplayer
    layers sit at 999+), background inert and focus kept inside for free.
  - The dialog spans the window and is transparent; .vpr-overlay and .vpr-box are
    what animate (::backdrop transitions are unreliable). Class toggles through
    $$.sm(el).class, end of animation by timer at config.speed.
  - Escape is handled on the dialog's keydown and stopped from propagating, because
    ModalDisplayer listens on document.body and would also close the panel beneath.
    The dialog's cancel event (phone back gesture) is turned into a normal cancel.
  - One dialog at a time across instances: a module-level queue.
  - The Promise resolves on the answer, before the exit animation.
  - Page freeze (overflow hidden + scrollbar compensation) restores the values it
    replaced, so a page already frozen by ModalDisplayer stays frozen.
  - danger focuses Cancel; input() focuses and selects the field; focus returns to
    the opener on close.
  - Strings are textContent, never innerHTML.

FOLLOW-UP (validator findings): freezePage() skips an already-held body; a "close"
listener and a disconnected-dialog check in next() settle externally closed dialogs;
null options and zero string widths throw the module's own errors.
